course: dictionary
lesson: 517
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word association can mean a group of people, a link in your mind, or being connected with something. Context tells you which meaning fits. Ask: what does the sentence say this is about?
explain: «Good zoos are accredited by associations such as the AZA in America, BIAZA in Britain and Ireland, EAZA in Europe and the ZAA in Australia, which check care, safety and conservation.» Here the associations are groups of people who check zoos, so the meaning is a group that joins together for a shared purpose.
explain: Association can also mean a link in your mind between two things. Say «sun» and you may think of «hot». That link is a word association. The sentence «blaming someone for being near is guilt by association» uses association to mean being connected with something, even when you did nothing wrong.
fact: An association is a group of people who join together for a shared purpose, like a club or society.
fact: An association can be a link or connection in your mind between two things, such as sun and hot.
fact: In maths and science, an association is a link between two sets of data shown on a graph.
fact: The phrase «in association with» means working together with someone or something.
fact: «Guilt by association» means being blamed because you are connected with a person or thing, even if you did nothing wrong.
exercise: «Good zoos are accredited by associations such as the AZA in America, BIAZA in Britain and Ireland, EAZA in Europe and the ZAA in Australia, which check care, safety and conservation.» What is an association in this sentence? | A ticket to enter a zoo | A type of animal found in zoos | A sort of food for zoo animals | *A group that checks zoos for care and safety
exercise: Maya hears «sun» and thinks of «hot». What is this link in her mind called? | A residents' association | A football association | *A word association | A graph of data
exercise: «Blaming someone for being near is guilt by association.» What does association mean here? | Being far away from something | A club for footballers | A graph on a page | *Being connected with someone or something
test: A residents' association is | *A group of people who live in the same area and join together for a shared purpose | A game played with a ball | A link between two sets of data on a graph
test: «The charity worked in association with the school.» What does «in association with» mean? | *Working together with | A type of graph for | Far away from | Being sad about
exam: Jo says association can only mean a graph. Why is she wrong? | *Association also means a group of people and a link in your mind between two things | Association means being sad | Association only means a type of animal | Association is only used in maths and never in English
